From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 00:01:02 +0200
Subject: media: sun6i-isp: Document the reach of the statistics grid

A zone spans width by height pixels of the frame but counts only width
by height/2 of them, sampling every other line. The grid therefore
reaches horz_num * width by vert_num * height, and that has to fit the
sensor.

Measured against 1600 by 1200 with an 8 by 8 grid: a zone of 200 by 150
reaches exactly the frame and all 64 zones come back at 15000 pixels. A
zone of 200 by 300 reaches 2400 lines, and exactly the four rows that
fit are written while the remaining rows still hold the previous
stream's values. Nothing reports the overrun, so a caller that gets this
wrong reads stale numbers that look plausible.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h | 14 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/uapi/sun6i-isp-config.h
@@ -138,9 +138,17 @@ struct sun6i_isp_params_config_drc {
  * HandleAeStat() divides each zone by the width times the height read
  * back out of the hardware's own saved AE_SIZE.
  *
- * The exposure zone covers width by height/2 pixels, again measured:
- * the sum is 254 * width * height / 2 to the pixel on a white field,
- * for every width from 64 to 384.
+ * A zone spans width by height pixels of the frame but only counts
+ * width by height/2 of them, sampling every other line: the sum is
+ * 254 * width * height / 2 to the pixel on a white field, for every
+ * width from 64 to 384.
+ *
+ * The grid therefore reaches horz_num * width by vert_num * height, and
+ * that has to fit the sensor. Tiling 1600 by 1200 with an 8 by 8 grid
+ * means 200 by 150, which gives all 64 zones at 15000 pixels. Ask for
+ * 200 by 300 instead and the grid wants 2400 lines, so only the four
+ * rows that fit are written and the rest of the array keeps whatever it
+ * held before -- the hardware reports no error for this.
  */
 struct sun6i_isp_params_config_h3a_window {
 	__u8	horz_num;
-- 
